      "claim": "The preference for better-corroborated theories is defensible on Popper's terms as a rational methodological choice based on verisimilitude (truth-likeness), not inductive probability. We prefer the theory that has withstood severe tests because it is the best candidate for truth we currently possess, even if we cannot assign it a higher probability of being true.",
